+            # compute_features_from_generator uses both to size the output memmap
+            # (open_memmap(..., shape=(n_total, ...))) and as its early-stop condition
+            # (`if row_counter >= n_total: break`). With augmentation_rounds > 1 that
+            # silently truncated every one of these four feature files back down to
+            # exactly one round's worth (verified: with augmentation_rounds=2 the
+            # positive_features_train.npy run stopped at precisely 71412 rows -- the
+            # tqdm total printed 71412//32 == 2231 batches -- discarding all of the
+            # second round's augmented clips instead of doubling the file as the v6
+            # config intends). Multiplying here keeps the memmap sized to what the
+            # generator actually produces.
+            aug_rounds = config["augmentation_rounds"]
+            compute_features_from_generator(positive_clips_train_generator,
